 "limitations": [
  {
   "wanted": "A metal 1/4\"-20 thumbscrew (or a captive camera screw) from the supplied hardware list",
   "blocked_by": "The catalog lists 1/4-20 only as an ASME B18.2.2 hex nut \u2014 there is no 1/4-20 screw in it",
   "why": "The screw that goes into a camera's socket is the one part of a quick-release plate that really wants to be metal: it is small, highly loaded, and threads into a metal socket, so a printed PLA thread is the weak link. I had to fall back on the salvaged webcam bolt (head shape unconfirmed) with a printed screw only as a spare."
  },
  {
   "wanted": "A soft rubber/TPU pad or a sheet of grip material for the plate's camera face",
   "blocked_by": "Only black high-speed PLA is available, and no grip material is in the hardware list",
   "why": "Real quick-release plates have a rubber face so the camera cannot rotate about the single screw. With PLA-on-camera friction only, a heavy or long lens can twist; I had to leave a note telling the user to add their own tape or a disc cut from a rubber band."
  }
 ],
